# Real Estate Gear Core

This repository contains the public, self-hostable core for a real estate portal:
a Next.js customer experience, an Express API, shared packages, Prisma
migrations, and an optional MLS worker. It is designed to run from one npm
workspace against PostgreSQL.

Commercial applications, private admin surfaces, client-specific products, and
private operational notes are not part of this repository.

## What Runs Here

The default local app is the portal at <http://localhost:3006>. It talks to the
API at <http://localhost:3001>, usually through same-origin `/api/*` rewrites.

PostgreSQL is required. Redis and Typesense can be added, but the base stack does
not depend on either service. The Agent API is present behind a guard and should
stay disabled unless a deployment explicitly opts in with `AGENT_API_ENABLED=true`.

## Services

| Location | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `apps/portal` | Public Next.js frontend for search, listings, inquiries, accounts, and favorites. |
| `apps/api` | Express service backed by Prisma and PostgreSQL. |
| `apps/mls-service` | Separate MLS synchronization process; dormant without board credentials. |
| `apps/typesense` | Optional search service tooling. |
| `packages/db` | Prisma schema, migrations, and guarded seed commands. |
| `packages/ui`, `packages/tokens` | Shared interface components and design tokens. |
| `packages/search`, `packages/cache`, `packages/email` | Optional infrastructure integrations used by the API and portal. |

## Local Setup

Use Node `>=22.12.0 <23` and npm. This project uses `package-lock.json`; do not
switch the workspace to pnpm or Yarn.

```bash
npm install
cp .env.example .env
npm run db:migrate
npm run dev
```

`npm run dev` starts the portal workflow, including the API process.

## Database Seeds

An empty PostgreSQL database is a supported starting point. Demo data is opt-in
and guarded by the exact database target from `DATABASE_URL`.

```bash
export CONFIRM_DEMO_SEED='<host>:<port>/<database>'
npm run db:seed:portal
npm run db:seed:demo-listings
```

Never configure demo seed confirmation in production. Guarded destructive reset
commands are available for local demo environments only.

## Daily Commands

```bash
npm run dev
npm run dev:api
npm run dev:portal
npm run dev --workspace=@realestategear/mls-service
npm run build:api
npm run build --workspace=portal
npm run test:api
npm run test:portal
npm run test --workspace=@realestategear/mls-service
npm run typecheck:api
npm run typecheck:portal
npm run typecheck:mls
```

For package publishing checks, use Node `22.14.0` or newer.

